ere to get  cameras into  you know different environments and  places and to get close to it  in ways that you haven't seen before um  yeah shooting inside vanguard was  was most of the experience really it  seems it feels like most of my memories  like me and fran  doing a sort of dosey doe inside the van  and  cursing ourselves that we didn't build  one on a stage or something  um but you know hopefully there's an  authenticity to shooting in those real  places so  hopefully it comes across chloe when i  watch these beautiful montages which  tell us so much about  fern's life and the way that she's  existing day to day  i think to myself i'm curious to know if  you had all of that kind of planned out  almost like in a storyboard form or was  it more of a question of  shooting as much as you could and then  dealing with all of that  in the editing room and putting it all  together then  i'd like to think that everything that i  have on screen is exactly how i planned  it and how i want it to be  yeah that would be a better answer but  no uh uh it was 50  50. we knew from very early on  that it's going to be not just a passing  through  space but also time um so we knew  we we plotted out the season changes  and the location the palette of the  location with desert  snow you know snow high desert low  desert  redwoods badlands you know we we planted  out  that route and then we we we um  scheduled the production according to  the season so for  for us um and then once we got there  it's really up to josh  to to find the most iconic image that  can represent  that place and then um you know in the  edit is trying to figure out  how to make us to feel like a year has  passed  with those little short montage and  having the  the diversity of space and seasons  was the only way to make that possible  molly your cast is made up of  seasoned performers like frances  mcdormand and david strathearn but also  some non-professional actors who are so  fantastic how did you go 